"DE-MILKJUG350V4WIDE-30012":{	"materials":["teflon coated food grade stainless steel"],"inv_date":"20241003","retail_price_cad":"47","weight":"185","dimensions_width":"8.5","sold":"560","hscode_default":"7323930060","ship_date":"2024-10-03","retail_price_aud":"49","retail_price_usd":"33","battery_chargeable":"0","ship_weight":"192","retail_price_gbp":"26","multi_liner":"[dt {The wide spout is best for beginner to intermediate latte artists, as it's much easier to make the standard latte art patterns.}] [dt {Milk spreads out wider, making full cup tulips and rosetta quite easily.}]   [dt {The wide spout tends to give you just one line width, and so demands less of the artist.}] [dt {On the other hand, the narrow spout is best for advanced latte artists, as it lets you draw very fine lines, as well as featuring linear control over the milk line width as you pour.}]\n\n<br><br>\n\n [dt {This milk jug size is the best size for single milk drinks.}] [dt {In addition, a common advanced latte art technique is to steam in a small milk jug, then transfer the milk to a larger jug for pouring latte art.}]\n\n<a href='\/blog\/for_beginner_and_intermediate_latte_artists_new_decent_milk_jugs'>[dt {More info on our blog}]<\/a>","url_shop":"milk_jug","retail_price_eur":"32","inventory_at_de":"770","dimensions_height":"10.5","retail_price_hkd":"260","dimensions_length":"11","one_liner":"330ml milk jug (wide spout)","morephotos":"milk jug v1v2 difference.jpg,DE-MILKJUG350V4WIDE-30012-spout-compare.jpg,DE-MILKJUG350V4WIDE-30012-bottom-compare.jpg,milkjug-330-01.jpg,milkjug-330-02.jpg,milkjug-330-03.jpg,jug-steaming.jpg,milk-01.avif,kit-02.avif"},
